const content="<article class=\"sn-page\" data-editorial-version=\"4\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine \u00b7 Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/boat-names-australia/logo.png\" alt=\"Boat Names Australia logo\" width=\"943\" height=\"220\" loading=\"lazy\"><h1>Boat Names Australia lettering for a yacht coming out of refit</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">When a boat is ashore for engine work, the hull is suddenly accessible in a way it rarely is at the mooring. Stand behind the stern and it&#x27;s easy to see why a tired name has been on the owner&#x27;s list for years. Boat Names Australia makes custom boat lettering and marine graphics. You can plan the new finish while the mechanical work is under way.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/boat-names-australia/photo.webp\" alt=\"Boat lettering from Boat Names Australia\" width=\"900\" height=\"413\" loading=\"lazy\"><section><h2>Save the details before polishing</h2><p>Take a straight-on picture of the old name and any emblem you want to retain. Put a measurement in the frame. On a classic motor cruiser the colour of an old stripe can be as distinctive as the shape of the letters. Send that material to the design team if you want a close match. If you want a fresh look, the online designer lets you preview actual wording and limit it to the length available.</p></section><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/boat-names-australia/detail.webp\" alt=\"Boat Names Australia lettering design service\" width=\"900\" height=\"413\" loading=\"lazy\"><section><h2>Look with the equipment back in place</h2><p>A bare stern on the hardstand has more apparent room than the same panel with a ladder, davits and tender aboard. Work from the area that stays visible. A long name might sit best on the quarters, with simpler home-port lettering astern. We like having the option to order separate layouts for those spaces instead of squeezing the same artwork onto both.</p><p>Registration lettering is supplied lined up on application paper. For a hull that has just been painted or polished, discuss surface preparation and timing with the supplier and yard before fitting. The goal is a finished set that looks as considered as the work underneath the engine cover.</p></section><p><a rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.boatnames.com.au/\">Design your boat lettering \u2197</a></p></div></article>";
